        },
        {
          "id": "docsStructure",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "GET STARTED\n\n1. Choose Examples and select Widget Playground or Signal Lab.\n2. Click Edit JavaScript to read the named event handlers.\n3. Press Run Panel to activate callbacks.\n4. Save/Export your own modified copy.",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 164,
          "width": 528,
          "height": 250,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 14
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "docsScript",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "JAVASCRIPT BASICS\n\nui.get(id) reads a widget.\nui.set(id,value) updates a widget.\nui.on(id,event,callback) registers a handler.\nplots.setSeries() displays computed data.\nplots.fromScope() transfers a real capture.",
          "x": 586,
          "y": 164,
          "width": 548,
          "height": 250,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 14
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "docsDesigner",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "MULTI-PAGE PROJECTS\n\nWidget Playground, Analog Charts and Chart Techniques contain multiple Pages. Their widgets share one script runtime, so switching Pages does not restart measurements.\n\nUse Properties and Design Tools to customize the layout.",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 438,
          "width": 528,
          "height": 220,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 14
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "docsBeta",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "HARDWARE SAFETY\n\nSimulation mode does not drive physical outputs. Before choosing Physical Device, check wiring and signal voltage limits.\n\nUse the explicit Start/Power On/Test actions in the instrument examples. Stop and release outputs when finished.",
          "x": 586,
          "y": 438,
          "width": 548,
          "height": 220,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 14
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "docsFooter",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "TIP: Examples are bundled as read-only Qt resources. Save/Export creates a normal editable .wfpanel file.",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 684,
          "width": 1110,
          "height": 44,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
